## 6. Engineering Observations

The simulation is used to investigate the following behaviours:

1. The diode conducts when it is forward biased.
2. The diode blocks current when it is reverse biased.
3. The output contains only one polarity of the input waveform.
4. The output is pulsating DC rather than a constant DC voltage.
5. The output frequency of a half-wave rectifier remains equal to the input frequency.

